.TH open_rwsync 3
.SH NAME
open_rwsync \- open a file for read/write with synchronization
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include "open.h"
.LP
int \fBopen_rwsync\fP(const char* \fIfilename\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B open_rwsync
opens the file named by \fIfilename\fP for reading and writing.
It attempts to set the O_SYNC and O_DIRECT flags on the file descriptor
to ensure synchronous I/O operations. Returns the file descriptor, or -1
on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
open(2), open_rw(3)